<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ma Xi'e</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 950–951 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ma Xi'e was ruler of Chu, a Ten Kingdoms state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hunan">Hunan</a>, from 950 to 951. An elder son of the founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ma-yin">Ma Yin</a>, he was passed over in favour of his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ma-xiguang">Ma Xiguang</a> in 947, rebelled from Langzhou and seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changsha">Changsha</a> at the end of 950. His misrule provoked a revolt that deposed him, and the Southern Tang occupied Hunan in 951, ending the Ma family's rule.</p></div>
